course: dictionary
lesson: 14505
title: Pelvic: a word about bodies and fish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special subject. «Pelvic» is one of them. It is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like the pelvic bones or the pelvic fin. Its meaning is "of or near the pelvis".
explain: The pelvis is the bowl-shaped group of bones at the bottom of your body. It joins your spine to your legs. «The X-ray showed the pelvic bones clearly.» Here pelvic tells you which bones were shown: the ones in that bowl at the bottom of the body.
explain: Pelvic has a second meaning in biology. «The goldfish moved its pelvic fins to turn slowly.» A pelvic fin is one of a pair of fins on the underside of a fish. When you meet a word in a new subject, check the context: are the words around it about bodies or about fish?
fact: Pelvic means of or near the pelvis.
fact: The pelvis is the bowl-shaped group of bones at the bottom of your body, joining your spine to your legs.
fact: A pelvic fin is one of a pair of fins on the underside of a fish.
fact: In health lessons, pelvic bones are also called the hips, and they support your body.
fact: «Her physio taught her some pelvic floor exercises.» Physiotherapists use the word pelvic when they talk about muscles near the pelvis.
exercise: «The X-ray showed the pelvic bones clearly.» What does pelvic mean here? | Of or near the head | *Of or near the pelvis, the bowl of bones at the bottom of the body | Shiny and bright | Very old and worn
exercise: «The goldfish moved its pelvic fins to turn slowly.» Where are pelvic fins on a fish? | At the very tip of its tail | Inside its mouth | On the top of its back | *Underneath the fish
exercise: «The pelvis joins the spine to the legs.» Find and copy one word that means the bowl of bones at the bottom of your body. | spine | body | legs | *pelvis
test: The pelvic bones support your body and join your spine to your legs. Where are they? | In your fingers | At the top of your head | *At the bottom of your body, near the hips | In your ears
test: «The fish flicked its pelvic fins under its belly.» Where are the pelvic fins on this fish? | At the tip of its nose | Along its back | *On the underside, near its belly | Inside its gills
exam: What is the pelvis, in plain words? | *The bowl of bones at the bottom of your body that joins your spine to your legs | A type of fish that lives in ponds | The small bones inside your fingers | The bones that protect your skull
